Synthetic NSE responses for tests/test_relations.py. They are hand-written, not saved from
NSE: field names and shapes follow public open-source NSE scrapers (corporates-pit,
historicalOR/bulk-block-short-deals, snapshot-capital-market-largedeal,
corporate-share-holdings-master, corporate-pledgedata) and have NOT yet been checked against a
live NSE response, because NSE was not reachable from the build environment. People, funds and
numbers are invented test values. __Dn__ is replaced by the test with the date n days ago
(dd-Mon-YYYY). Replace or extend these with real responses once www.nseindia.com is allowed.
collect_relations_india.py --replay writes only to an explicit scratch MB_ROOT (one holding a
.scratch-ok file, with no .git, CLAUDE.md or price files; no write target may resolve outside
its own data/ or into a repo checkout, be hard-linked, or share an inode with a file in the
code checkout's data/). These checks guard against accidental writes into a real data/ tree;
they are not a security boundary against someone deliberately constructing a scratch root.
